From e29b23bfd4f13dbcebe71b2225242f24d805014c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Le Duc <baptiste.le-duc@vates.tech>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:41:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] set-memory-uc: keep the test result when restoring WB on
 exit

The 1.0.7 to 2.0.1 update of test-ring0 now overwrites `ret` by storing
set_memory_wb() result in it, so any failure detected by the test is
discarded and the test reports success as long as the final restore to WB
works.

Store the result of the restoring set_memory_wb() in a separate `err`
and return the test result in `ret`, falling back to `err` only when the
test itself passed, so a failure already stored in `ret` is not
overwritten.

If the restore fails, the direct-map PTE may still be UC/WC and the UC
memtype reserved by set_memory_uc() is not released. Freeing the page would
hand that to the next user of the page, leading to a memory type mismatch
with any WB alias. Leak the page instead, as dma-direct and swiotlb do when
set_memory_encrypted() fails.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Baptiste Le Duc <baptiste.le-duc@vates.tech>
---
 linux/set-memory-uc/set-memory-uc.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/linux/set-memory-uc/set-memory-uc.c b/linux/set-memory-uc/set-memory-uc.c
index ee86e77..8cdec2b 100644
--- a/linux/set-memory-uc/set-memory-uc.c
+++ b/linux/set-memory-uc/set-memory-uc.c
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ static int set_memory_uc_run(struct xst_test *test)
 	pte_t *pte;
 	u64 val;
 	unsigned int level;
-	int ret = 0;
+	int ret, err;
 
 	t->stats.pte_before = 0;
 	t->stats.pte_uc = 0;
@@ -149,7 +149,11 @@ static int set_memory_uc_run(struct xst_test *test)
 	}
 
   out:
-	ret = set_memory_wb((unsigned long)virt, 1);
+	err = set_memory_wb((unsigned long)virt, 1);
+	if (err) {
+		pr_err("set_memory_wb() failed when restoring WB, leaking page\n");
+		return ret ?: err;
+	}
 	__free_page(page);
 	return ret;
 }
